<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66909" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετα-ρρέω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταρρῠήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					7.573
				</span></i>
			:—<i>flow differently: change to and fro, ebb and
				flow</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ Εὔριπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1167b7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>change from one side to the other</i>, as from right to left,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				193d
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>change sides, transfer one's allegiance</i>
			or <i>affections</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. πᾶν τὸ ἔθνος εἰς αὐτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					1.4.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πράγματα μ. εἰς Μιθριδάτην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Posidon.
					36
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταρρυῆναι εἰς παῖδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					3.38
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>VS</u>
				2.3
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
